winewayland: announce no keyboard layout before there is a keymap

When a surface gains text input focus, the driver posts
WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST with the IME variant of the current layout. Before
the compositor has sent a keymap, or on a seat with no keyboard, there is no
current layout: the driver posted 0xe0010000, an IME layout whose language is
0. WinForms answers that message by building a CultureInfo from the language,
which throws CultureNotFoundException ("0 (0x0000) is an invalid culture
identifier"). Power BI Desktop showed that exception twice at start, behind
which the report never loaded.
Seen under GNOME (mutter 50.6, headless with a virtual monitor and no input
device, Fedora 44 container, 2026-11-27); WINEDEBUG=+keyboard showed
"Changing keyboard layout to 0xffffffffe0010000".
Post nothing until a layout exists, on text input focus or on keyboard
focus (which posted layout 0). set_current_xkb_group activates the layout,
with the IME state, when the keymap arrives, as before.
Applies after wine-11.18-composition.patch.
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_keyboard.c
@@ -112,7 +112,12 @@
 
 void activate_keyboard_hkl(HWND hwnd, BOOL ime)
 {
-    HKL hkl = ime && !is_ime_hkl(keyboard_hkl) ? get_ime_hkl(LOWORD(keyboard_hkl)) : keyboard_hkl;
+    HKL hkl;
+
+    /* No keymap yet, or no keyboard at all: there is no layout to announce.
+     * set_current_xkb_group activates one, with the IME state, when it comes. */
+    if (!keyboard_hkl) return;
+    hkl = ime && !is_ime_hkl(keyboard_hkl) ? get_ime_hkl(LOWORD(keyboard_hkl)) : keyboard_hkl;
     TRACE("Changing keyboard layout to %p\n", hkl);
     NtUserPostMessage(hwnd, WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST, 0 /*FIXME*/, (LPARAM)hkl);
 }
@@ -804,8 +809,9 @@
     keyboard->focused_hwnd = hwnd;
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&keyboard->mutex);
 
-    NtUserPostMessage(keyboard->focused_hwnd, WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST, 0 /*FIXME*/,
-                      (LPARAM)keyboard_hkl);
+    if (keyboard_hkl)
+        NtUserPostMessage(keyboard->focused_hwnd, WM_INPUTLANGCHANGEREQUEST, 0 /*FIXME*/,
+                          (LPARAM)keyboard_hkl);
 
     if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return;
 
